.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Aug 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-service-unexpose - Revoke a service exposed on the AceTeam Network gateway


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel service unexpose  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops serving /expose// on this node's gateway and deletes its saved
record, so the service is unreachable now AND does not come back the next time
the node restarts.

.PP
Any outstanding 'link' tokens for the service stop working, because the gateway
fails closed for a name with no exposure policy.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unexpose


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Stop sharing the nvr module's Frigate UI
  citadel service unexpose frigate
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-service(1)\fP
